WEBVTT

00:05.390 --> 00:11.990
Let's talk about tailoring the project management processes you already know that you don't have to

00:11.990 --> 00:15.380
use every process on every project.

00:15.380 --> 00:21.320
But then we also have to make a determination as to what depth we should utilize the processes that

00:21.320 --> 00:27.680
are selected and then we can even tailor those processes to fit the type of projects that we're managing

00:27.950 --> 00:33.770
or our organization or what's most important to us in our project or endeavor.

00:34.160 --> 00:36.290
So let's talk about tailoring the processes.

00:36.290 --> 00:39.750
First off there are four key facts that we need to know.

00:39.800 --> 00:45.080
The first one is what processes are we going to use on the project.

00:45.080 --> 00:50.930
So I know I don't have to use all the processes but which ones should I use or will we be using in this

00:50.930 --> 00:52.250
project.

00:52.280 --> 00:54.330
The second one is to what depth.

00:54.350 --> 00:59.590
So if we know we have to do a managed quality process.

00:59.760 --> 01:06.920
But what does that mean exactly to what depth to what extent or we're going to do risk analysis of qualitative

01:06.920 --> 01:14.230
and quantitative risk analysis to what depth if it's a large high profile project.

01:14.260 --> 01:19.730
Typically I'm going to go deeper and more intense in those processes.

01:19.730 --> 01:26.590
A small low priority project pretty high level I don't either invest a lot of time at all these processes.

01:26.590 --> 01:33.460
So depending what the project is the priority of the project and the process that we selected will make

01:33.460 --> 01:40.300
a determination as to how intense to what depth to what extent do we do that process.

01:40.300 --> 01:44.530
We already know Step 3 Not every process is needed on every project.

01:44.530 --> 01:45.520
So that's a given.

01:45.520 --> 01:47.300
Now we've got that down.

01:47.800 --> 01:54.240
Typically though Step 4 The larger the project the more processes are likely.

01:54.280 --> 02:01.790
So the bigger the project probably you're going to touch a lot more processes than a small project.

02:02.650 --> 02:08.470
A few more things about tailoring in the Pinback guy throughout the Pinback I will see this idea of

02:08.470 --> 02:14.560
tailoring a process or tailoring processes and these will be in the different knowledge areas chapters

02:14.560 --> 02:20.890
starting in chapter 4 on integration management all the way to 13 on stakeholder management.

02:21.190 --> 02:24.040
So what we'll see here Step 1 will be knowledge areas.

02:24.040 --> 02:28.030
So each knowledge area will be some tailoring that can happen.

02:28.030 --> 02:35.400
We know processes step to here processes live inside of knowledge areas and then step three Tailleur

02:35.410 --> 02:37.680
those to fit your project.

02:37.900 --> 02:44.350
So it's the project the priority the project the characteristics of the project that will tell us which

02:44.350 --> 02:51.220
processes we need and to what extent do we need those processes and then Step Number four the fourth

02:51.220 --> 02:57.670
thing to know throughout the Pinback guide as I mentioned we'll see an opportunity to do tailoring.

02:57.670 --> 03:00.440
So just be aware that don't let that throw us.

03:00.440 --> 03:07.240
We knew through these chapters and tailoring comes back again every knowledge area every process has

03:07.240 --> 03:09.740
an opportunity to be tailored.

03:09.760 --> 03:18.320
All right I'll see you in the next lecture.
